---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Stewpot Ledger — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 84"
  description="Chullin 84: slide your fortune from a hundred dinars to ten thousand and watch Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya's stewpot fill with vegetables, fish, or meat — then guess the bracket for six purses, diagnose a cup of lukewarm water, and flip five household maxims from Proverbs."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0f0b08] !text-[#ecdfc9]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#2c2115] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#1c1409]/80 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#d0973f]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#f2b95a]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 84 · 2026-07-23
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">🍲 The Stewpot Ledger</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-xl !text-[#f2b95a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">יֹאכַל אָדָם וְיִשְׁתֶּה פָּחוֹת מִמַּה שֶּׁיֵּשׁ לוֹ</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
        Chullin 84 finishes the technical laws of covering the blood and then turns, unexpectedly, into a page
        of household economics. Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya draws a ladder: a person's stewpot should hold
        vegetables, fish, or meat depending on exactly how many dinars he has —
        <strong class="!text-[#ecdfc9]">and three generations of sages can't agree how strictly to keep it.</strong>
        Slide your fortune. Fill your pot. Then see if you can predict the bracket.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Context card ============ -->
      <div class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#141109] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">before you slide — how the daf gets here</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2416] bg-[#100c07] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a]">🪤 Trap your own</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
              The mitzva to cover a kill's blood is written "who <em>traps</em>" — yet the law reaches tame fowl
              too, like geese and chickens that never roam. The extra word teaches <em>derech eretz</em>:
              a person shouldn't eat meat as a matter of course (84a:17–18).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2416] bg-[#100c07] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a]">🍖 Only for craving</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
              "You may eat meat" (Deut. 12:20) only when your soul craves it — not from the marketplace out of
              habit, and not by slaughtering your only cow or your only sheep (84a:19–20).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2416] bg-[#100c07] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a]">💰 The dinar ladder</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
              From here, Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya sets four real brackets — a hundred dinars, a thousand, five
              thousand, ten thousand — each with its own stewpot (84a:21).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2416] bg-[#100c07] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a]">🫖 Know your generation</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
              Rav, Rabbi Yochanan, and Rav Nachman each read the ladder differently — each one frailer than the
              last (84a:22).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Main game: Stewpot Ladder ============ -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#171009] p-5">
        <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">the stewpot ladder</p>
          <div class="flex gap-1.5 text-[11px] font-bold">
            <button id="tab-explore" class="rounded-lg border border-[#d0973f]/50 px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#f2b95a]">explore</button>
            <button id="tab-predict" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#8c8271] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">predict</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="explore-panel"></div>
        <div id="predict-panel" class="hidden"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Cup wizard ============ -->
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#171009] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">bonus toy — diagnose your cup</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
          Rabbi Yochanan: better to drink from <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">כָּסָא דְּחָרָשִׁין</span> —
          a cup a witch has handled — than from a cup of lukewarm water, which he calls genuinely dangerous.
          But he immediately narrows the warning three times over (84b:2). Answer honestly.
        </p>
        <div id="cup-wizard" class="mt-4"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Five verses flip gallery ============ -->
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#171009] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">five verses for the household — Proverbs 27:26–27 (84a:23–24)</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">Tap a phrase to see what the Gemara reads out of it.</p>
        <div id="verse-grid" class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#141109] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">learn the real daf</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
          Chullin 84 opens by closing out the mishna's puzzle over covering the blood: consecrated birds and
          animals are excluded from <em>kisui hadam</em> through a web of derivations — Rav Yosef reads the
          mishna as blending Rabbi Meir and Rabbi Shimon, the Gemara mines "וְשָׁפַךְ וְכִסָּה" and "חַיָּה אוֹ
          עוֹף," and the heretic Ya'akov challenges Rava that if a wild animal counts as domesticated for
          kashrut signs, a domesticated animal's blood should count as a wild animal's for covering too — Rava
          answers that its blood is compared to water, which prompts the Gemara to ask whether that same
          comparison lets one immerse impure items in blood, closed off by three exclusions folded into the
          verse "מַעְיָן... וּבוֹר... מִקְוֵה מַיִם"
          (<a class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84a.1">84a:1–16</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
          Then comes the ladder this game is built from — the trapping law's lesson in restraint, Rabbi Elazar
          ben Azarya's four brackets, and Rabbi Yochanan's frugal-living and cup-of-lukewarm-water advice
          (<a class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84a.17">84a:17</a>–<a class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84b.4">84b:4</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">
          The daf closes on a live dispute: Rav Eina rules that one who slaughters for a critically ill person
          on Shabbat must cover the blood — Rabba calls it an astonishing error. Rabbi Yosei tries a <em>kal
          va'chomer</em> from circumcision to show the covering of a <em>koy</em>'s blood can't override a
          Festival; the Sages volley back with the shofar of Rosh Hashana, and Rabbi Elazar HaKappar the
          Distinguished lands the refutation that stands
          (<a class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84b.5">84b:5–14</a>).
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#d0973f]/40 bg-[#d0973f]/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a] hover:bg-[#d0973f]/20">Chullin 84 on Sefaria →</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.84a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Rashi (×66)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.84a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Steinsaltz (×39)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Chullin.84a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Rabbeinu Gershom (×33)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Chullin.84a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Ritva (×14)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank {
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }
    input[type='range'] {
      -webkit-appearance: none;
      appearance: none;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #2c2115;
      outline: none;
    }
    input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-thumb {
      -webkit-appearance: none;
      appearance: none;
      width: 22px;
      height: 22px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #f2b95a;
      border: 3px solid #171009;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    input[type='range']::-moz-range-thumb {
      width: 22px;
      height: 22px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #f2b95a;
      border: 3px solid #171009;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .fade-in { animation: fadeIn 0.35s ease both; }
      @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
      .pot-swap { transition: background-color 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease; }
    }
    .flip-card { perspective: 1000px; }
    .flip-inner {
      position: relative;
      transform-style: preserve-3d;
      transition: transform 0.5s;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .flip-inner { transition: none; }
    }
    .flip-card.flipped .flip-inner { transform: rotateY(180deg); }
    .flip-front, .flip-back {
      backface-visibility: hidden;
      -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
    }
    .flip-back { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform: rotateY(180deg); }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

    // ==================================================================
    // Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya's ladder — Chullin 84a:21, ref for all four
    // brackets. Below the top bracket, the item is eaten weekly, "from
    // Shabbat eve to Shabbat eve" (84a:21). The top bracket eats meat daily.
    // ==================================================================
    const LADDER_REF = 'Chullin 84a:21';
    const LADDER_URL = 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84a.21';
    const BRACKETS = [
      { min: 100, item: 'vegetables', icon: '🥬', color: '#7fae59', freq: 'weekly', he: 'לִיטְרָא יָרָק' },
      { min: 1000, item: 'fish', icon: '🐟', color: '#5f9cc4', freq: 'weekly', he: 'לִיטְרָא דָּגִים' },
      { min: 5000, item: 'meat', icon: '🥩', color: '#c1553e', freq: 'weekly', he: 'לִיטְרָא בָּשָׂר' },
      { min: 10000, item: 'meat', icon: '🥩', color: '#e0a83a', freq: 'daily', he: 'קְדֵרָה בְּכׇל יוֹם' },
    ];

    function bracketFor(dinars) {
      let b = BRACKETS[0];
      for (const cand of BRACKETS) if (dinars >= cand.min) b = cand;
      return b;
    }

    function fmt(n) {
      return n.toLocaleString('en-US');
    }

    const GENERATIONS = [
      {
        who: 'Rav', tag: 'the elder’s word',
        quote: 'צְרִיכִין אָנוּ לָחוֹשׁ לְדִבְרֵי זָקֵן',
        text: '"We must heed the words of the elder." Rav takes Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya’s ladder seriously — spend on food exactly as it says, no more.',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rabbi Yochanan', tag: 'my father was made of sturdier stock',
        quote: 'אַבָּא מִמִּשְׁפַּחַת בְּרִיאִים הֲוָה',
        text: '"Abba (Rav) came from a family of healthy people — but people like us, whoever has a peruta in his pocket should rush it to the storekeeper." One generation down, austerity gets dangerous.',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rav Nachman', tag: 'we borrow and eat',
        quote: 'כְּגוֹן אָנוּ לוֹוִין וְאוֹכְלִין',
        text: '"People like us borrow money and eat." Two generations later, even Rabbi Yochanan’s caution has become a luxury.',
      },
    ];

    // ---- Explore panel ----
    let dinars = 1000;

    function potCard(dinars) {
      const b = bracketFor(dinars);
      return `
        <div class="pot-swap fade-in rounded-xl border p-4 text-center" style="border-color:${b.color}66; background:${b.color}14;">
          <p class="text-4xl">${b.icon}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold" style="color:${b.color}">Your pot holds: ${b.item}</p>
          <p class="frank text-lg !text-[#f2b95a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${b.he}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#b6ab93]">${b.freq === 'daily' ? 'Every single day — a pot on the stove daily.' : 'Once a week — from Shabbat eve to Shabbat eve.'}</p>
        </div>`;
    }

    function renderExplore() {
      $('explore-panel').innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-center text-3xl font-black !text-[#ecdfc9]">${fmt(dinars)} <span class="text-sm font-normal !text-[#8c8271]">dinars</span></p>
        <input id="dinar-slider" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="0" class="mt-3 w-full" aria-label="Your fortune in dinars" />
        <div class="mt-2 flex justify-between text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#6b6153]">
          <span>100</span><span>1,000</span><span>5,000</span><span>10,000</span><span>20,000</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4">${potCard(dinars)}</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs !text-[#8c8271]">Source: <a href="${LADDER_URL}" class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]">${LADDER_REF}</a></p>
        <div class="mt-5 border-t border-[#2c2115] pt-4">
          <p class="text-center text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">whose caution do you trust?</p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
            ${GENERATIONS.map((g, i) => `<button data-gen="${i}" class="gen-btn rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">${g.who}</button>`).join('')}
          </div>
          <div id="gen-reveal" class="mt-3"></div>
        </div>`;

      const slider = $('dinar-slider');
      // Log-scale slider: t in [0,100] maps to dinars in [100, 20000].
      const valueFromT = (t) => Math.round(100 * Math.pow(200, t / 100));
      const tFromValue = (v) => (100 * Math.log(v / 100)) / Math.log(200);
      slider.value = String(Math.round(tFromValue(dinars)));
      slider.addEventListener('input', () => {
        dinars = valueFromT(Number(slider.value));
        document.querySelector('#explore-panel > p').innerHTML = `${fmt(dinars)} <span class="text-sm font-normal !text-[#8c8271]">dinars</span>`;
        const potHost = $('explore-panel').children[3];
        potHost.innerHTML = potCard(dinars);
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('.gen-btn').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const g = GENERATIONS[Number(btn.dataset.gen)];
          $('gen-reveal').innerHTML = `
            <div class="fade-in rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] p-3 text-left">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a]">${g.who} — "${g.tag}"</p>
              <p class="frank mt-1 text-base !text-[#cfc4a4]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${g.quote}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">${g.text}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] !text-[#6b6153]">Chullin 84a:22</p>
            </div>`;
        });
      });
    }

    // ---- Predict panel: guess-the-bracket quiz ----
    const ROUNDS = [
      { dinars: 400 },
      { dinars: 1000 },
      { dinars: 4000 },
      { dinars: 5000 },
      { dinars: 9999 },
      { dinars: 10000 },
    ];
    let roundIdx = 0;
    let quizScore = 0;
    let picked = null; // item picked this round

    function renderPredict() {
      if (roundIdx >= ROUNDS.length) return renderPredictEnd();
      const round = ROUNDS[roundIdx];
      const items = [
        { key: 'vegetables', icon: '🥬', label: 'Vegetables' },
        { key: 'fish', icon: '🐟', label: 'Fish' },
        { key: 'meat', icon: '🥩', label: 'Meat' },
      ];
      $('predict-panel').innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">round ${roundIdx + 1} of ${ROUNDS.length} · score ${quizScore}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-center text-2xl font-black !text-[#ecdfc9]">A man has ${fmt(round.dinars)} dinars.</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-center text-xs !text-[#8c8271]">What goes in his stewpot?</p>
        <div id="item-choices" class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-3 gap-2">
          ${items.map((it) => `<button data-item="${it.key}" class="item-btn rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-2 py-3 text-center text-xs font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:border-[#d0973f]/50 hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]"><span class="block text-2xl">${it.icon}</span>${it.label}</button>`).join('')}
        </div>
        <div id="freq-choices" class="mt-3"></div>
        <div id="predict-verdict"></div>`;
      document.querySelectorAll('.item-btn').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          picked = btn.dataset.item;
          document.querySelectorAll('.item-btn').forEach((b) => (b.disabled = true));
          btn.classList.add('border-[#d0973f]');
          $('freq-choices').innerHTML = `
            <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs !text-[#8c8271]">How often does it reach the pot?</p>
            <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
              <button data-freq="weekly" class="freq-btn rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Once a week (Shabbat)</button>
              <button data-freq="daily" class="freq-btn rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Every single day</button>
            </div>`;
          document.querySelectorAll('.freq-btn').forEach((fb) => {
            fb.addEventListener('click', () => finishRound(picked, fb.dataset.freq));
          });
        });
      });
    }

    function finishRound(item, freq) {
      const round = ROUNDS[roundIdx];
      const b = bracketFor(round.dinars);
      const ok = item === b.item && freq === b.freq;
      if (ok) quizScore++;
      $('predict-verdict').innerHTML = `
        <div class="fade-in mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4 ${ok ? 'border-[#7fae59]/50 bg-[#7fae59]/10' : 'border-[#c1553e]/50 bg-[#c1553e]/10'}">
          <p class="frank text-lg font-bold ${ok ? '!text-[#a9cf8b]' : '!text-[#e08c7d]'}">${ok ? '✓ Correct' : '✗ Not quite'}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#d8d1c0]">
            With ${fmt(round.dinars)} dinars, Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya's ladder says: ${b.icon} <strong class="!text-[#ecdfc9]">${b.item}</strong>,
            ${b.freq === 'daily' ? 'a pot every single day.' : 'once a week, from Shabbat eve to Shabbat eve.'}
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#8c8271]">Source: <a href="${LADDER_URL}" class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]">${LADDER_REF}</a></p>
          <button id="btn-next-round" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#d0973f]/50 bg-[#d0973f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#f2b95a] hover:bg-[#d0973f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#f2b95a]">${roundIdx === ROUNDS.length - 1 ? 'See your standing →' : 'Next purse →'}</button>
        </div>`;
      $('btn-next-round').addEventListener('click', () => {
        roundIdx++;
        picked = null;
        renderPredict();
      });
      $('btn-next-round').focus();
    }

    function renderPredictEnd() {
      let title;
      if (quizScore === ROUNDS.length) title = 'You have the ladder memorized';
      else if (quizScore >= ROUNDS.length - 2) title = 'A sound grasp of the brackets';
      else title = 'The brackets are trickier than they look';
      $('predict-panel').innerHTML = `
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#d0973f]">final score</p>
          <p class="frank mt-2 text-3xl font-black !text-[#ecdfc9]">${quizScore} / ${ROUNDS.length}</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg !text-[#f2b95a]">${title}</p>
          <button id="btn-requiz" class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-[#d0973f]/50 bg-[#d0973f]/15 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold !text-[#f2b95a] hover:bg-[#d0973f]/25">Try the purses again</button>
        </div>`;
      $('btn-requiz').addEventListener('click', () => {
        roundIdx = 0;
        quizScore = 0;
        renderPredict();
      });
    }

    // ---- Tabs ----
    function activateTab(tab) {
      const exploreBtn = $('tab-explore');
      const predictBtn = $('tab-predict');
      if (tab === 'explore') {
        $('explore-panel').classList.remove('hidden');
        $('predict-panel').classList.add('hidden');
        exploreBtn.className = 'rounded-lg border border-[#d0973f]/50 px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#f2b95a]';
        predictBtn.className = 'rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#8c8271] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]';
      } else {
        $('predict-panel').classList.remove('hidden');
        $('explore-panel').classList.add('hidden');
        predictBtn.className = 'rounded-lg border border-[#d0973f]/50 px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#f2b95a]';
        exploreBtn.className = 'rounded-lg border border-[#2c2115] px-2.5 py-1 !text-[#8c8271] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]';
      }
    }
    $('tab-explore').addEventListener('click', () => activateTab('explore'));
    $('tab-predict').addEventListener('click', () => activateTab('predict'));

    // ==================================================================
    // Bonus toy: diagnose your cup — Rabbi Yochanan's lukewarm-water rule
    // (Chullin 84b:2). Danger only when: metal vessel AND unflavored AND
    // unboiled. Any one exception makes it safe.
    // ==================================================================
    const CUP_URL = 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.84b.2';
    let cupStep = 'vessel';
    let cupAnswers = {};

    function renderCup() {
      const host = $('cup-wizard');
      if (cupStep === 'vessel') {
        host.innerHTML = `
          <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#ecdfc9]">What is the cup made of?</p>
          <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
            <button id="cup-metal" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">🥣 Metal</button>
            <button id="cup-earthen" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">🏺 Earthenware</button>
          </div>`;
        $('cup-metal').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.vessel = 'metal'; cupStep = 'flavor'; renderCup(); });
        $('cup-earthen').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.vessel = 'earthen'; cupStep = 'result'; renderCup(); });
      } else if (cupStep === 'flavor') {
        host.innerHTML = `
          <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#ecdfc9]">Metal it is. Did you cast flavorings (spices, herbs) into the water?</p>
          <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
            <button id="cup-flav-yes" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">🌿 Yes, flavored</button>
            <button id="cup-flav-no" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Plain water</button>
          </div>`;
        $('cup-flav-yes').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.flavor = 'yes'; cupStep = 'result'; renderCup(); });
        $('cup-flav-no').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.flavor = 'no'; cupStep = 'boiled'; renderCup(); });
      } else if (cupStep === 'boiled') {
        host.innerHTML = `
          <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#ecdfc9]">Plain water, in metal. Was the water boiled?</p>
          <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
            <button id="cup-boil-yes" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">🔥 Yes, boiled</button>
            <button id="cup-boil-no" class="rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] px-3 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#b6ab93] hover:!text-[#ecdfc9]">Never boiled</button>
          </div>`;
        $('cup-boil-yes').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.boiled = 'yes'; cupStep = 'result'; renderCup(); });
        $('cup-boil-no').addEventListener('click', () => { cupAnswers.boiled = 'no'; cupStep = 'result'; renderCup(); });
      } else {
        const danger = cupAnswers.vessel === 'metal' && cupAnswers.flavor === 'no' && cupAnswers.boiled === 'no';
        let why = '';
        if (cupAnswers.vessel === 'earthen') why = 'Rabbi Yochanan’s warning applies only "בִּכְלִי מַתָּכוֹת" — in metal vessels. Earthenware was never a problem.';
        else if (cupAnswers.flavor === 'yes') why = 'Even in metal, flavorings cast into the water clear the danger.';
        else if (cupAnswers.boiled === 'yes') why = 'Even plain water in metal is fine once it has been boiled.';
        else why = 'Metal vessel, unflavored, unboiled — every leniency runs out. This is the one combination Rabbi Yochanan actually meant.';
        host.innerHTML = `
          <div class="fade-in rounded-xl border p-4 text-center ${danger ? 'border-[#c1553e]/50 bg-[#c1553e]/10' : 'border-[#7fae59]/50 bg-[#7fae59]/10'}">
            <p class="text-3xl">${danger ? '⚠️' : '✅'}</p>
            <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg font-bold ${danger ? '!text-[#e08c7d]' : '!text-[#a9cf8b]'}">${danger ? 'Danger — pour it out' : 'Safe to drink'}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b6ab93]">${why}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] !text-[#8c8271]">Source: <a href="${CUP_URL}" class="!text-[#f2b95a] underline hover:!text-[#f9d38a]">Chullin 84b:2</a></p>
            <button id="cup-reset" class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-[#d0973f]/50 bg-[#d0973f]/15 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold !text-[#f2b95a] hover:bg-[#d0973f]/25">Diagnose another cup</button>
          </div>`;
        $('cup-reset').addEventListener('click', () => { cupStep = 'vessel'; cupAnswers = {}; renderCup(); });
      }
    }

    // ==================================================================
    // Five verses flip gallery — Proverbs 27:26–27, derash at Chullin 84a:23–24
    // ==================================================================
    const VERSES = [
      {
        phrase: 'כְּבָשִׂים לִלְבוּשֶׁךָ',
        translit: '"The lambs will be for your clothing"',
        lesson: 'Your clothing should come from the shearing of your own lambs — raise the flock that dresses you, rather than buying clothes outright.',
      },
      {
        phrase: 'וּמְחִיר שָׂדֶה עַתּוּדִים',
        translit: '"And goats the worth of a field"',
        lesson: 'A person should always sell a field to buy goats — never sell goats to buy a field. A flock earns; land sits.',
      },
      {
        phrase: 'וְדֵי חֲלֵב עִזִּים',
        translit: '"And goats’ milk enough"',
        lesson: 'It is enough for a person to live off the milk of the kids and lambs already inside his own house — contentment with what you keep.',
      },
      {
        phrase: 'לְלַחְמְךָ לְלֶחֶם בֵּיתֶךָ',
        translit: '"For your food, for the food of your household"',
        lesson: 'The verse names your own food first: secure your own footing before you can provide for a household.',
      },
      {
        phrase: 'וְחַיִּים לְנַעֲרוֹתֶיךָ',
        translit: '"And sustenance for your maidens"',
        lesson: 'Mar Zutra bar Rav Nachman: give plain sustenance to your children — a parent should not accustom a child to meat and wine.',
      },
    ];

    function renderVerses() {
      $('verse-grid').innerHTML = VERSES.map((v, i) => `
        <div class="flip-card" style="height:150px;">
          <div class="flip-inner" style="height:100%;">
            <button data-i="${i}" class="flip-front absolute inset-0 flex w-full flex-col items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-[#2c2115] bg-[#100c07] p-3 text-center hover:border-[#d0973f]/50">
              <span class="frank text-lg !text-[#f2b95a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${v.phrase}</span>
              <span class="mt-1 text-[10px] !text-[#6b6153]">${v.translit}</span>
              <span class="mt-2 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#8c8271]">tap to reveal</span>
            </button>
            <div class="flip-back flex flex-col items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-[#d0973f]/40 bg-[#1c1409] p-3 text-center">
              <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#d8d1c0]">${v.lesson}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('.flip-front').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => btn.closest('.flip-card').classList.toggle('flipped'));
        btn.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
          if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); btn.click(); }
        });
      });
    }

    renderExplore();
    renderPredict();
    renderCup();
    renderVerses();
  </script>
</Layout>
